                <pb facs="0568" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg472"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 228.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">notes of director of the patent bureau.</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Nukiyama, agent for Maurice Russell, a British subject.</p>
                <p>Trade-mark, “Eagle Brand,”</p>
                <p>Application dated May 4, 1898.</p>
                <p>Preliminary rejection of application, June 25, 1898.</p>
                <p>No further steps were taken by parties interested, so that the rejection was made
                    final on August 26, 1898.</p>
                <p>The “Swiss Milk” trade-mark is registered in the name of Maurice Russell as his
                    own property, as proved by documents in my office.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
